rands comprising Narellan, CoverStar, Radiant, and GLI brands. The company was formerly known as Latham Topco, Inc. and changed its name to Latham Group, Inc. in March 2021. Latham Group, Inc. was founded in 1956 and is headquartered in Latham, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Sean  Gadd B.E., BEng, M.B.A. | President, CEO & Director | Age 52","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $287K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $20K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Latham Group, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $973M market cap on $546M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -8% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are expanding by +2.8pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 31%.","The business throws off $38M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 5.70\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 6.7% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.09149742537037862},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Financial quality scores above most Industrials peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Latham Group (NASDAQ:SWIM) Stock Rating Raised to \u201cHold\u201d at Zacks Research","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/latham-group-nasdaqswim-stock-rating-raised-to-hold-at-zacks-research.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794402939.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.875,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"GOLDFISH SWIM SCHOOL HONORS TOP FRANCHISEES AT OWNERS' CELEBRATION AS THE BRAND REACHES 20TH ANNIVERSARY","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-rele